From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:04:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: route subtitle, Hub route chip and privacy line in
 Contacts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

People design (contacts-people-titan2):

* Route subtitle: under each local contact, the default number as
  before followed by the person's other routes, "Mail" when they have an
  email address and "Messages" when Sable Messages is installed and they
  have a number ("Mobile · +1 555 0101 · Mail · Messages"). Email
  presence comes from one bounded read-only Email query in a new loader
  next to the numbers loader; nothing is written.
* Locked and private states: while the device is locked or Sable private
  mode is on (Sable Hub > Connected apps, read from Hub's read-only
  org.sableos.hub.privacy provider; observed, and re-read on resume),
  the number is left out ("Phone · Mail · Messages") and a line above the
  list says why: "12 people · Details hidden until unlock" ("3 people
  matched · …" in search) or "Private mode · Numbers hidden". Without
  Hub there is no private mode.
* Message route chip: QuickContact gets a "Message" toolbar action,
  shown when Sable Messages is installed and the person has a number; it
  opens the conversation for the default number (else the first) in Sable
  Messages (ACTION_SENDTO smsto:, package org.sableos.messages; Sable
  Hub's inbox is Sable Start's Hub page). It only navigates.

ContactsProvider stays the owner of contact data; editing, linking and
accounts are unchanged.
